# desktop-amd64.pkgs — NCZ-OS AMD64 desktop offline closure. FULL closure,
# self-contained (a build consuming this file alone gets the complete
# package set) — NOT a diff-only/divergence-only file.
#
# Derived from manifests/desktop.pkgs (the Sky1/arm64 desktop closure) by the
# 2026-09-14 AMD64-line package audit (see docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-AUDIT.md for
# full per-package reasoning, and for the classification-count table this
# file's sections correspond to: DROPPED / KEPT-AS-IS / GENERIC-FIRMWARE /
# x86-microcode / T2-conditional / GPU-vendor-conditional). The DROPPED
# section below documents what was REMOVED from the Sky1 closure and why;
# everything else in this file (the large "KEPT AS-IS" block onward) is the
# actual portable closure content, listed in full, not summarized.
#
# Consume the same way as desktop.pkgs: grep -vE '^\s*(#|$)'.

# ============================================================================
# DROPPED — Sky1/CIX-chip-specific, no AMD64 equivalent needed
# ============================================================================
# chromium-ncz-sky1  — our custom V4L2-M2M hardware-decode Chromium build for
#                       the Linlon VPU. Operator decision 2026-09-14: do not
#                       build/ship a custom Chromium for AMD64 at all. Use
#                       google-chrome-stable + Vivaldi only (both below).
# ncz-ffmpeg         — Sky1 VPU-accelerated ffmpeg (see docs/AMD64-PACKAGE-
#                       AUDIT.md "ffmpeg parity" section). NOT arch-portable;
#                       needs its own AMD64 hwaccel build (VAAPI/NVENC), which
#                       is NOT YET BUILT — see follow-on work in the audit doc.
#                       Do not add ncz-ffmpeg itself to this manifest; a
#                       future ncz-ffmpeg-amd64 (or similar) package name goes
#                       here once that build exists. Stock `ffmpeg` (already
#                       below, from the r189.4 bucket) covers software
#                       encode/decode in the meantime.
# libdrm-radeon1, libdrm-nouveau1, libdrm-freedreno1, libdrm-tegra0,
# libdrm-etnaviv1    — these were pulled into the Sky1 closure only as
#                       transitive Mesa dependency noise for architectures
#                       NCZ-OS does not target; irrelevant to AMD64's own
#                       real AMD/Intel/NVIDIA DRM backends (amdgpu/i915/
#                       nouveau ship their own libdrm backends via
#                       mesa-vulkan-drivers below). Not carried forward.

# ============================================================================
# KEPT AS-IS (portable, unchanged from desktop.pkgs)
# ============================================================================
greetd
