# Intel VA-API driver (iHD) for Gen8+ Intel iGPUs -- Broadwell and newer,
# including the CoffeeLake UHD 630 in T2 Macs and the iGPU on generic Intel
# desktops/laptops. Debian main package; provides
# /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/dri/iHD_drv_video.so, which libva selects for
# i915/xe render nodes. The Mesa runtimes pulled in elsewhere (mesa-va-drivers)
# only carry the non-Intel VA backends (radeonsi/nouveau/...), so an Intel-only
# machine has no VA-API decode path at all without this package.
# amd64 ONLY -- arm64/Sky1 decodes through the CIX VPU (V4L2/M2M), not VA-API.
# Already claimed in build/arch-parity-allowlist.tsv (desktop/intel-media-va-driver,
# amd64-only); pinned present by sbom/expected-packages-amd64.txt and
# build/test-amd64-intel-vaapi.sh. Do not add to desktop.pkgs.
intel-media-va-driver
mesa-vulkan-drivers
mesa-opencl-icd
libglu1-mesa

# Online Accounts UI backend. post-install/20-desktop.sh runs on BOTH
# platforms and does `apt-get install -y gnome-online-accounts`, but until
# this entry no seed provided it, so on an offline install that call could
# only fail and the Online Accounts UI had nothing to talk to (KNOWN-ISSUES
# #4). Seeded here rather than in desktop.pkgs because the package is
# amd64-only: gnome-online-accounts 3.58.1-2 is published for amd64 and is
# absent from the arm64 published index, and Sky1 has no Online Accounts
# requirement. Claimed in build/arch-parity-allowlist.tsv
# (desktop/gnome-online-accounts, amd64-only).
gnome-online-accounts
clinfo

